From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:06:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: add H.264 encoding for the V3s and the
 A10/A20

Add an encoder video device to the reworked driver: the encoder
infrastructure and the V3/V3s/S3 H.264 encoder by Paul Kocialkowski
(Bootlin, cedrus/h264-encoding branch), plus support for the A10/A20
H.264 encoder:

- A20 register differences from the V3s block (engine select per job,
  put-bits polling, PARA1/ME_PARA/ME_INFO layout, a real MV buffer,
  second line buffer, sub-pixel and reconstruction buffer sizes),
  picture sizes up to 1920x1088, any even width and height;
- encoder drain (V4L2_ENC_CMD_STOP, LAST flag, EOS event), picture
  queue buffers returned in stop_streaming, defaults that stock
  userspace (FFmpeg h264_v4l2m2m) works with;
- frame-level rate control (V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FRAME_RC_ENABLE,
  _BITRATE, _BITRATE_MODE CBR): an integer-only port of the quadratic
  JM model used by Allwinner's A20 libvencoder, with I-frame QP from the
  previous GOP's P QPs, open GOP, all-intra and buffer overflow recovery;
- correct VUI frame rate, several robustness fixes;
- reset the VE when the role of the next job (decode/encode) differs
  from the previous one: interleaved decode and encode sessions
  otherwise make decode jobs time out every few seconds.

Based on work by Paul Kocialkowski <paul.kocialkowski@bootlin.com>
(Bootlin) and on Jens Kuske's research on the A20 video engine.

Tested on Cubieboard2 and Cubietruck (A20): encoding up to 1920x1080
with FFmpeg h264_v4l2m2m, simultaneous decode and encode.

Tested on a Rikomagic MK802 (A10): every encoded stream is bit-identical
to the A20 output.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
